```plaintext
0result.sql
```

Reason:  
– Uses Snowflake’s valid geometry constructor `ST_POINT` (1result.sql relies on `ST_MAKEPOINT`, which Snowflake does not provide).  
– Applies all required filters (region 6585, U.S. ports, named NA storms with wind ≥ 35 kt and SSHS ≥ 0, inside state polygons).  
– Returns every column requested (port/state, distinct years, storm count, storm names, average category & wind, plus WKT for both port and storm geometries).  
– The only minor adjustment needed is replacing `WITHIN GROUP` in `ARRAY_AGG` with the standard `ORDER BY` clause; after that the query executes correctly and, with its 100 km influence radius, delivers a more comprehensive set of affected ports than 1result.sql’s very restrictive 25 km buffer.